<!--- initialize the myArray Array --->
<bx:set myArray = []>

<!--- This is a different way which also works 
    to create the array to contain the 4 structures
        <!--- append the 4 separately defined structures to myArray  --->
        <bx:set myArray.append(bookOne)>
        <bx:set myArray.append(bookTwo)>
        <bx:set myArray.append(bookThree)>
        <bx:set myArray.append(bookFour)>
--->

<!---
    This is a different way which also works to create the 
    array to contain the 4 structures
        <!--- append the 4 separately defined structures to myArray  --->
        <bx:set myArray = [ bookOne, bookTwo, bookThree, bookFour ] />
--->


<!--- 
    This is a different way which also works to create the 
    array to contain the 4 structures
        <!--- assign each of the 4 separately defined structures
            to individual indices of myArray  --->
        <bx:set myArray[1] = bookOne>
        <bx:set myArray[2] = bookTwo>   
        <bx:set myArray[3] = bookThree>
        <bx:set myArray[4] = bookFour>
--->


<!--- added after class chat session 11-10-2026 to create myArray and all 5 structures in one step, 
    with assistance from GitHub Copilot AI --->
<br />
<p><strong>Added after class chat session 11-10-2026</strong> create array with structures in one step,
    also changed the <code>genre</code> key to <code>genres</code> and made it an array of strings for each book. Then use
    a loop to display info about each book and tally up and display the total price. Also added the fifth book
    from the Excel file.</p>
<bx:set myArray = [
    {
        basicInfo: {
